TAM-HIDE - WORKSTATION PRIVACY FOR TAMLINUX

tam-hide locks a Tamlinux workstation cleanly and without disclosing account
or session details.

Version 0.3.1 builds on Phase P1 (0.0.0-0.2.2) with Phase P2a workstation
readiness and Phase P2b disposable KVM `tam-pane` DRM/KMS verification:

- Privileged Argon2id (`libargon2`, default m=65536 KiB, t=2, p=1) salted
  slow-hash passcode store (`passcode_store`, `tam-hidectl passcode-*`) with
  constant-sweep matching across all accounts and atomic hot-reload
  (`RELOAD_STORE`, `tam-hidectl reload-store`, `SIGHUP`).
- `tam-hided` automatic `seat0` session discovery via `libsystemd` `sd-login`
  (`USE_SYSTEMD?=1`, `--no-logind` / `USE_SYSTEMD=0` portable fallback),
  compositor lock-confirmation gate, fail-closed return to `lock_vt` when an
  active session ends, and privilege-separated `auth.sock` with `SO_PEERCRED`
  gating, server-side exponential lockout, and single-use 128-bit `PICK` tokens.
- Interactive non-disclosing console passcode and multi-account picker prompt
  on `lock_vt` (`tty7`, outside `systemd-logind`'s `NAutoVTs=6` / `ReserveVT=6`
  range) inside `tam-hided` (`--no-vt-prompt` opt-out).
- `tam-hide` Wayland `ext-session-lock-v1` locker for `tam-pane` with idle
  output blanking/wake, automatic `/run/tam-hide/auth.sock` + `XDG_VTNR`
  discovery (seamless PAM fallback when `tam-hided` is absent; `--pam-only`
  opt-out), cross-VT `AUTH_HANDOFF`, and post-auth `LOCK_UI_PICKER`.

Phase P2b (`upstream/2026-11-27-phase-p2b-tam-pane-vm-verification.md`)
verified `0.3.1` end-to-end with `tam-pane` on DRM/KMS, `sd-login`, the `tty7`
console prompt, and `SIGHUP` reload in a disposable Arch KVM guest. Installing
`tam-hided.service` on a live workstation remains gated on Fred's explicit
approval and a recorded rollback point.

Follows the tam-idol 1.3.0 standard.

WHERE THINGS ARE

  src/        Wayland locker (tam-hide), VT seat controller (tam-hided), CLI (tam-hidectl)
  tests/      unit tests and headless tam-pane integration test
  sandbox/    nested tam-pane demo for manual verification
  arch/       security and compositor design
  plans/      implementation phases
  work/       current handoff and session records
  ROADMAP.md  planned milestones
  UPSTREAM.md upstream code and references
